# Cross-platform line endings.
#
# Every text file is checked out with LF on every OS, whatever core.autocrlf
# says. Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which would give
# CRLF: biome (lineEnding "lf") then fails `bun run lint` on the whole tree,
# shell scripts get a `bash\r` shebang that does not run, and the migrations
# leak CRLF into the generated embedded.ts. Git detects binaries itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never convert.
*.node binary
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
